# flake fix: run_test.go's Execute tests write an executable `java` script and exec it. A fork
# in a sibling test inherited the parent's open write descriptor, so the exec failed ETXTBSY
# ("text file busy") under concurrent load. A package-level mutex now spans the script write and
# its exec. go test -count=100 ./pkg/tlc/ is ok (71s); before the fix -count=50 was red.
